 "食い込む": "[to bite into (e.g. rope into skin) ; to cut into]\nمثال: 医者の費用は本当に貯金に食い込む。\n→ Doctors' bills really cut into our savings. / اِخْتَلَسَ, أَزْعَجَ (To intrude unrightfully on someone else’s rights or territory.)  [to encroach] / [to be wedged (i.e. underwear pulled from the back, driving it between the buttocks)]",
 "食い違い": "فَرْق, اِخْتِلَاف (The quality of being different.) / فَرْق, فُرُوق (A characteristic of something that makes it different from something else.) / خِلاف, خِلافات (A disagreement or argument.) / فَرْق (The result of a subtraction; sometimes the absolute value of this result.) / مَيَّزَ (To distinguish or differentiate.)  [difference]\nمثال: ２人の意見には大きな食い違いがあった。\n→ There was a great gap between the views of the two.",
