 "食む": "أَكَلَ imperfective: يَأْكُلُ, كَلْ (To ingest.)  [to eat (fodder, grass, etc.)]\nمثال: 牛が野原で草をはんでいた。\n→ Cattle were grazing in the field. / اِسْتَقْبَلَ, اِسْتَلَمَ (To take, as something that is offered; to accept.) / اِسْتَقْبَلَ, يَسْتَقْبِل (To act as a host for guests; to give admittance to; to permit to enter, as into )  [to receive (a salary)]",
 "食らいつく": "قَضَمَ (Chiefly followed by at, away, or on: to take a small, quick bite, or several of )  [to nibble]\nمثال: しかし今は、一目見て、サメがその人にくらいつくのは避けられないようだということに気づかずにはいられない。\n→ However, I can't help noticing, at this moment, that at first glance it seems inevitable that the shark will devour the man. / [to get one's teeth into (metaphorically) ; to get to grips with]",
 "食らい付く": "قَضَمَ (Chiefly followed by at, away, or on: to take a small, quick bite, or several of )  [to nibble]\nمثال: しかし今は、一目見て、サメがその人にくらいつくのは避けられないようだということに気づかずにはいられない。\n→ However, I can't help noticing, at this moment, that at first glance it seems inevitable that the shark will devour the man. / [to get one's teeth into (metaphorically) ; to get to grips with]",
 "食らう": "أَكَلَ imperfective: يَأْكُلُ, كَلْ (To ingest.)  [to eat]\nمثال: 毒を食らわば皿まで。\n→ As well be hanged for a sheep as a lamb. / اِسْتَقْبَلَ, اِسْتَلَمَ (To take, as something that is offered; to accept.) / اِسْتَقْبَلَ, يَسْتَقْبِل (To act as a host for guests; to give admittance to; to permit to enter, as into )  [to receive (e.g. a blow)]\nمثال: 昔は、悪いことをすると、学校の先生から平手をくらったり拳固をもらうことが当たり前だった。\n→ In the past it was perfectly normal to get the back of a teacher's hand or fist as punishment. / [to be on the receiving end (of something undesirable) ; to undergo (trouble)]\nمثال: 銀行強盗すると懲役１０年食らうぞ。\n→ Bank robbery will cost you ten years in prison.",
 "食らわす": "اِتِّفَاقِيَّة (An agreement between parties; an arrangement.)  [to deal (a blow)]\nمثال: 私は彼のあごに１発食らわしてやった。\n→ I landed him a blow on the chin.",
 "食らわせる": "[to make someone eat] / اِتِّفَاقِيَّة (An agreement between parties; an arrangement.)  [to deal (a blow)]\nمثال: 彼が謝ろうとしていたちょうどそのとき、その人は彼の顔にパンチをくらわせた。\n→ He was about to apologize when the man punched him in the face.",
 "食わす": "أَطْعَمَ, غَذَّى (To give (someone or something) food to eat.)  [to feed (e.g. an animal on oats)] / دَعَمَ, دَعَّمَ (To help keep from falling.) / أَيَّدَ, دَعَمَ (To back or favor a cause, party, etc., mentally or with concrete aid) / تَأْيِيد, دَعْم (Financial or other help.)  [to support (e.g. a family)] / اِتِّفَاقِيَّة (An agreement between parties; an arrangement.)  [to deal (e.g. a blow)]\nمثال: ジムは映画に行く約束をしたガールフレンドに待ちぼうけをくわされ、雨の中を一時間も待たされて頭にきている。\n→ Jim's angry because his date for the movie stood him up and he wasted an hour waiting for her in the rain. / خَدَعَ, غَشَّ (To trick or mislead.)  [to deceive]",
 "食わせる": "أَطْعَمَ, غَذَّى (To give (someone or something) food to eat.)  [to feed (e.g. an animal on oats)]\nمثال: あのレストランはひどいものを食わせる。\n→ They serve terrible food at that restaurant. / دَعَمَ, دَعَّمَ (To help keep from falling.) / أَيَّدَ, دَعَمَ (To back or favor a cause, party, etc., mentally or with concrete aid) / تَأْيِيد, دَعْم (Financial or other help.)  [to support (e.g. a family)]\nمثال: 彼はポールがまちぼうけをくわせたのだと悟った。\n→ He realized Paul had stood him up. / اِتِّفَاقِيَّة (An agreement between parties; an arrangement.)  [to deal (e.g. a blow)]\nمثال: 彼は敵に不意打ちを食わせた。\n→ He surprised his opponent. / خَدَعَ, غَشَّ (To trick or mislead.)  [to deceive]",
