 "駄目": "عَدِيمُ الْفَائِدَةِ (Without use or the possibility to be used.)  [useless]\nمثال: 去年はジョギングシューズを２足駄目にした。\n→ I wore out two pairs of jogging shoes last year. / عَبَثًا, سُدًى (Without success or a result; ending in failure.)  [in vain]\nمثال: もうだめだ。\n→ It's all over. / عَجَزَ, لَا يَسْتَطِيع (Can not; be unable to (whether due to physical inability, logical impossibility,)  [cannot]\nمثال: 夜遅くまで起きていては駄目だよ。\n→ Don't sit up late at night. / [neutral point ; intersection owned by neither player at the end of a game]",
 "駄目になる": "أَفْسَدَ (To ruin; to damage in such a way as to make undesirable or unusable.) / دَلَّلَ, غَنَّجَ (To ruin the character of, by overindulgence; to coddle or pamper to excess.) / فَسَدَ, نَتِنَ (To go bad; to become sour or rancid; to decay.)  [to spoil]\nمثال: 彼女のブーツは私のものよりずっと早くだめになる。\n→ Her boots wear out much more quickly than mine.",
 "駄目を押す": "تَأَكَّدَ (To make oneself certain (of something, or that something is the case); to verify)  [to make sure]\nمثال: あいつまた待ち合わせの時間に遅れてくるかもしれないから、集合は７時だって駄目を押しておいてよ。\n→ He's likely to be late so you'd better tell him again that the meeting time is seven to make double sure.",
 "駄目人間": "فَشَل, قُصُور (State or condition of not meeting a desirable or intended objective, opposite of) / فَشَل (An object, person or endeavour in a state of failure, has failed at something or) / عُطْل (Termination of the ability of an item to perform its required function; breakdow)  [failure]",
