 "高い": "عَالٍ, اَلْعَالِي (Physically elevated, extending above a base or average level:) / مَسْطُول (Intoxicated; under the influence of a mood-altering drug, formerly usually alcoh)  [high]\nمثال: 銀行はリスクの高い顧客へのローンには高い金利をつける。\n→ Banks charge higher interest on loans to risky customers. / غَالٍ, الْغَالِي (Having a high price or cost.)  [expensive]\nمثال: そんな高い車を買う余裕はありません。\n→ I can't afford to buy such an expensive car. / عَالٍ, اَلْعَالِي (Physically elevated, extending above a base or average level:) / مَسْطُول (Intoxicated; under the influence of a mood-altering drug, formerly usually alcoh)  [high (level)]\nمثال: 新しい製造過程は高い歩留まりを可能にする。\n→ The new production process achieves a high yield. / عَالٍ, اَلْعَالِي (Noisy.)  [loud]",
 "高が": "وَحِيد (1. alone in a category) / فَقَط (Without others or anything further; exclusively.) / فَقَط (No more than; just.) / فَقَط (Introduces a clause with negative polarity, often one which upsets the listener')  [only]\nمثال: 彼はたかが政治屋だ。\n→ He is not any better than a politician.",
